    <label>Sotisi</label>
    <description>When Sotisi awoke among the ruins, the first ray of sunlight to fall upon the old Yelu City landed on her shoulder.

As someone who had lost her memory, surviving beneath this land was no easy task. Yet, relying on experience she could not remember learning and on guidance from somewhere beyond reason, Sotisi survived. She crossed through underground worlds both dark and magnificent, met many Ningsha who had become wanderers through disaster or isolated by calamity, and glimpsed a once-glorious age in countless ruins and the songs of travelers.

She could not accept a world in decline, nor bear to watch her kin fall one after another before her eyes, so she decided to act. Drawing on instinctive knowledge, she taught wanderers how to find water, survey underground veins, and discover habitable caves; she taught secluded villages to cultivate farmland again and forged spear and shield for fragile settlements to defend themselves. Erosion followed like a shadow. Faceless yet powerful entities always arrived after her and destroyed many wanderer camps and isolated villages, but... without her help, fewer would have survived, would they? This era was difficult enough as it was.

She will offer you some help, guide more Ningsha to join your colony, and find ways to buy you time after incidents occur. But Erosion will be even more eager to visit your colony, and Sotisi's abilities are limited. Faced with a worsening tide of events, even she can do little.</description>
